#: src/macros/streams.md:6
msgid "Token Streams"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:8
msgid ""
"A **token stream** is a sequence of token trees. It is the fundamental input "
"and output format for both declarative and procedural macros in Rust:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:11
msgid ""
"**Macro Input:** The tokens passed inside the brackets of the macro "
"invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:13
msgid ""
"**Macro Output:** The new tokens returned by the macro that replace the "
"macro invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:16
msgid ""
"For declarative macros, the output is structured not just as a token stream, "
"but also must be syntactically valid Rust. The generated syntax is inserted "
"into the AST of the program where the macro is invoked."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:21
msgid ""
"// The input token stream does not need to be valid Rust syntax, as long as "
"it\n"
"// tokenizes (which requires any brackets to be balanced).\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:30
msgid ""
"// The macro returns tokens: 1 + 2\n"
"    // Since expansion inserts a structured AST fragment, precedence is "
"preserved!\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:32
msgid "\"3 * 10 = {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:32
msgid "// Outputs \"30\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:36
msgid ""
"Because macro output is inserted as an AST subtree, we don't need to wrap "
"expansions in safety parentheses (unlike C macros, where literal replacement "
"would cause `1 + 2 * 10` to equal `21`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:43
msgid ""
"This slide shows `macro_rules!` defining a declarative macro. We do not need "
"to visit this in detail yet, as we will do so on the next slide."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:45
msgid ""
"Explain that a Token Stream can contain arbitrary sequences of tokens. The "
"tokens do not need to form valid Rust code on their own (for example, "
"`special_print!(#foo(bar:123))` uses `#` and `:` in custom ways)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/streams.md:48
msgid ""
"When a macro expands, the _emitted_ token stream must make syntactic sense "
"at the position where the macro is invoked."
msgstr ""
